<title>UK: INSIGHT -STERLING/MARK SEEN SUPPORTED AROUND 2.96.</title>
<headline>INSIGHT -STERLING/MARK SEEN SUPPORTED AROUND 2.96.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sterling's skid to below 2.97 marks and $1.58 on Thursday has left the unit vulnerable to fresh falls but support around 2.96-2.95 marks and $1.5860 should hold, said chartists.</p>
<p>&quot;I think sterling is heading for a pause after its dramatic falls this week,&quot; said Nick Shamin, currency analyst at ANZ Investment.</p>
<p>At 0735 GMT, sterling/mark was trading at 2.9800/10 against 2.9690/00 in late Europe on Thursday and off earlier lows of 2.9625. Cable was at $1.5915/25 against $1.5880/90 in late Europe and off session lows around $1.5870.</p>
